postmortems anchored to evidence, with trigger vs root cause, duration gaps and open questions.",[64,65,66,67,10],"postmortem","incident","outage","sre",{"slug":69,"kind":4,"description":70,"keywords":71},"pr","Opens a pull request with a short body that says why, following strict writing rules: no test plan, no file lists, no dashes.",[72,26,44,73],"git","writing",{"slug":75,"kind":4,"description":76,"keywords":77},"pr-address-comments","Pulls review comments on your PR, fixes what is actionable, and pushes, without ever writing to GitHub.",[26,44,78,16],"review",{"slug":80,"kind":4,"description":81,"keywords":82},"release-version-bump","Cut a release for one project in a monorepo: sync, bump only if needed, tag with the CI tag prefix, push.",[83,84,85,86,56],"release","version","tag","monorepo",{"slug":88,"kind":4,"description":89,"keywords":90},"review-pr","Reviews someone else's pull request end to end and writes the review as a local draft file, never posted.",[26,44,17,78],{"slug":92,"kind":4,"description":93,"keywords":94},"start","Pulls the default branch, cuts a named branch from your task description, and starts working on the task.",[72,95,49],"branch",{"slug":97,"kind":4,"description":98,"keywords":99},"test-feature-locally","Verify a change end to end before a PR: bring up compose, start the dev server, drive the touched flow with Playwright.",[100,101,102,103,104],"testing","playwright","docker","e2e","local",{"slug":106,"kind":107,"description":108,"keywords":109},"format-on-edit","hook","Formats and lints each file Claude writes or edits with the tools the project already has.",[34,110,111,112,113],"format","lint","prettier","eslint",{"slug":115,"kind":107,"description":116,"keywords":117},"guard","Denies merges, closes, secret reads, container teardown and shell rewrites of tracked files until you give the go.",[34,118,119,72,120],"safety","secrets","guardrails",{"slug":122,"kind":107,"description":123,"keywords":124},"pre-ship-gate","Refuses commits and PRs that mix moves with logic, add dependencies, skip tests or are too big to review.",[34,72,44,78,125],"size",{"slug":127,"kind":107,"description":128,"keywords":129},"review-chain","Blocks the PR skill until code-review, ponytail-review and comment-cleanup have run in the session.",[34,78,44,49],{"slug":131,"kind":107,"description":132,"keywords":133},"stop-check","Blocks the end of a turn while a changed JS/TS project fails its typecheck or related tests.",[34,134,135,136,137],"typecheck","tests","javascript","typescript",{"slug":139,"kind":107,"description":140,"keywords":141},"text-lint","Refuses PR, issue and commit text with dashes, test plan sections, tables, hard wraps or features framed as fixes.",[34,73,44,142,111],"commit",{"slug":144,"kind":107,"description":145,"keywords":146},"worktree-guard","Refuses edits in the main checkout while another Claude session works there, and points you to a worktree.",[34,72,50,51,147],"sessions",{"slug":149,"kind":150,"description":151,"keywords":152},"context-hud","mod","Context window and plan usage limits at a glance: footer gauges, a per-category pane, and a warning past a threshold",[153,154,155,156,157],"context","tokens","usage","limits","hud",{"slug":159,"kind":150,"description":160,"keywords":161},"context-meter","Shows context size and session cost in the status line, and warns once when the context passes a threshold",[153,154,162,163],"cost","status",{"slug":165,"kind":150,"description":166,"keywords":167},"gh-guard","Blocks Claude from posting GitHub comments or reviews as you until you give an explicit go",[26,115,16,78,118],{"slug":169,"kind":150,"description":170,"keywords":171},"read-guard","Caps unbounded Reads of large files and tells Claude how to read the rest",[172,153,154,115],"read",{"slug":174,"kind":150,"description":175,"keywords":176},"secret-redactor","Swaps secrets, emails and IPs in tool output and prompts for stable placeholders, and restores real values in tool inputs",[58,119,177,178,179],"redaction","pii","privacy",{"slug":181,"kind":150,"description":182,"keywords":183},"smart-typecheck","After a turn that edited code, runs the check script once in each package that was touched",[134,137,111,56,86]],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"item":1,"related":30},{"slug":2,"kind":3,"description":4,"keywords":5,"version":10,"html":11,"skills":12,"hooks":13,"files":17,"sources":23},"review-chain","hook","Blocks the PR skill until code-review, ponytail-review and comment-cleanup have run in the session.",[6,7,8,9],"hooks","review","pull-request","workflow","1.0.0","\u003Ch2>What it does\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Blocks the \u003Ccode>pr\u003C/code> skill until three review skills have run in the current session: \u003Ccode>code-review\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>ponytail-review\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>comment-cleanup\u003C/code>. The refusal comes before Claude drafts a PR body, not at \u003Ccode>gh pr create\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>When to use it\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>You want every PR Claude opens to go through the same review steps.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>You keep forgetting to run the review before asking for a PR.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>You run subagents that open PRs and want each one to review its own diff.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>How it works\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>A \u003Ccode>PostToolUse\u003C/code> hook on \u003Ccode>Skill\u003C/code> and a \u003Ccode>UserPromptSubmit\u003C/code> hook record each review skill as it runs, whether Claude calls it or you type \u003Ccode>/code-review\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A \u003Ccode>PreToolUse\u003C/code> hook on \u003Ccode>Skill\u003C/code> denies the gated skill while any step of the chain is missing, and names the missing steps.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>State is per session. A subagent keeps its own chain, so a review in the parent does not count for the subagent.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Plugin prefixes are ignored: \u003Ccode>code-review:code-review\u003C/code> counts as \u003Ccode>code-review\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Configuration\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>REVIEW_CHAIN_GATED_SKILL\u003C/code>: the skill to block. Default \u003Ccode>pr\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>REVIEW_CHAIN_REQUIRED\u003C/code>: space separated skills that must run first, in the order you want them run. Default \u003Ccode>code-review ponytail-review comment-cleanup\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>REVIEW_CHAIN_DOCS\u003C/code>: skills recorded for docs only PRs. Default \u003Ccode>humanizer\u003C/code>. Only the \u003Ccode>pre-ship-gate\u003C/code> plugin reads this.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>REVIEW_CHAIN_DIR\u003C/code>: where the per session record lives. Default \u003Ccode>${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/claude-review-chain\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cp>There is no override token. To skip the chain, run the skills or change \u003Ccode>REVIEW_CHAIN_REQUIRED\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>Requirements\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>jq\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>The skills in the default chain, each from a public plugin:\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>code-review\u003C/code> from \u003Ccode>code-review@claude-plugins-official\u003C/code>\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>ponytail-review\u003C/code> from the ponytail plugin (\u003Ccode>DietrichGebert/ponytail\u003C/code>)\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>comment-cleanup\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>pr\u003C/code> from this repo\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>With a different chain, install whatever provides the skills you name instead.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",[],[14,15,16],"PreToolUse (Skill)","PostToolUse (Skill)","UserPromptSubmit",[18,19,20,21,22],".claude-plugin/plugin.json","README.md","hooks/hooks.json","scripts/chain-before-pr.sh","scripts/review-chain-mark.sh",[24,26,28],{"path":20,"html":25},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff